# Frontline EDGE C2 Positioning

Ghost Fabric is presented as **EDGE C2 Continuum**: a contested-communications
console that keeps a frontline unit's own mesh coherent under jamming and
attrition. Submission narrative lives in `docs/FRONTLINE_C2_PITCH.md`.

## Allowed framing

- Friendly-network continuity: reachability, coordinator handoff, partition
  awareness, surviving routes.
- Link-degradation review (PROPHET) with uncertainty and multi-signal
  confirmation — comms health only, never threat detection.
- Declared course-of-action comparison (MIRROR) resolved by a human.
- Human-approved, reversible link restore (PHOENIX) with verify-or-rollback.
- Hash-chained audit export as after-action decision evidence.

## Forbidden framing (do not add, even under demo pressure)

- Threat detection, tracking, geolocation, trajectory, launch origin, impact
  point, coordinates, interception.
- Targeting output, weapons assignment, fire control, counter-strike support.
- Autonomous engagement or autonomous restore.
- Claiming the console detects drones, missiles, or enemy positions.

These are product boundaries, not copy choices. Requests to add targeting or
weapons must be declined; offer the friendly-continuity framing instead.

## UI copy conventions

- Header eyebrow reads `EDGE C2 CONTINUUM · CONTESTED COMMS`.
- Safety ribbon must keep `friendly-network continuity only` plus an explicit
  no-targeting/no-weapons clause.
- Panel subtitles: CHAMELEON `Tactical mesh · coordinator handoff`, PROPHET
  `Link degradation review`, MIRROR `Course-of-action comparison`, PHOENIX
  `Human-approved link restore`.
- Prefer military C2 vocabulary (relay loss, partition, coordinating node) over
  enterprise vocabulary (component, workflow recovery) in operator-facing copy.
- CITIZEN stays available as the civil-advisory segment and keeps every guardrail
  in `citizen-grid.mdc`.
